Z||000040||Fiero_Freak||04-24-2001||11:53 PM||||I definately had the ass end stick out there.  Was coming to an intersection as the light changed.  The car in front of my took off, but he instantly killed it.  I didn't notice that as I was hammering it to get around the semi on the right.  When I did see him I swerved to the right lane and the ass end kept going right.  I laid into the throttle and it seems to be sticking until I let off.  It kept coming around to the right.   As I spun the semi drove past my hood at about 40 and I ended up backwards on the concrete center divider watching the world go by.  Not the best way to break in your new tires.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
